​Privacy Policy
​Effective Date: October 28, 2026
​This Privacy Policy applies to the Kids Play mobile application (hereinafter referred to as the "App").
​We respect the privacy of all users, especially children and parents, and are committed to protecting any information associated with the use of our App.
​1. Information We Do Not Collect
​No Personal Information: We do not collect, store, or share any personal information (such as names, email addresses, phone numbers, or precise location data) from users, including children.
​No Account Required: Users can access all features and learning modules of the App without creating an account or registering.
​2. Local Data Storage
​The App uses local device storage (localStorage) solely to save local game scores, selected classes, and learning progress locally on your device.
​This data remains strictly on your device and is never transmitted, uploaded, or shared with us or any third-party servers.
​3. Children's Privacy (COPPA Compliance)
​Our App is designed to be a safe, educational tool for children.
​Because we do not collect personal information from children under 13 (or any users), our App complies fully with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and related child privacy standards.
​4. Third-Party Services and Advertisements
​The App does not integrate third-party analytics trackers, ad networks, or external data collection tools.
​5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
​We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date. We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically.
